  { question: 'Can beginners use a weightlifting app?', answer: 'Yes, if the app explains technique, starts with manageable volume and gives users a way to adjust exercises and resistance. Beginners should prioritize movement quality and consistency over testing maximum strength.' },
  { question: 'How many days per week should a beginner strength train?', answer: 'Many beginners can make progress with two or three full-body sessions each week. The appropriate schedule depends on experience, goals, other activity, recovery and health circumstances.' },
  { question: 'Do I need a full gym?', answer: 'No. Useful programs can be built around bodyweight, resistance bands, dumbbells or a complete gym. The app should make equipment requirements clear before a workout begins.' },
